## Station Architecture

1. `server.py` implements the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over standard I/O (stdio).
2. Interacts with ComfyUI via HTTP loopback (`http://127.0.0.1:8188`, configurable via `COMFYUI_URL`):
   - `POST /prompt`: submit workflow execution graph
   - `GET /history/{prompt_id}`: query execution status and output artifacts
   - `GET /queue`: monitor pending and running executions
   - `GET /view`: fetch generated image/audio buffers
   - `GET /system_stats`: read device and process memory stats
3. Station safety policies:
   - `guard_submits()` intercepts every workflow submission before calling `POST /prompt`.
   - VRAM gate checks (`vram.py`) evaluate model weights and workload hints.
   - On unmetered systems without workstation telemetry, returns `UNKNOWN` and refuses rather than issuing an unmeasured permit.
   - Outbound network tools (`view_image` with remote URLs) withheld unless approved via `IRSOFKA_COMFY_ALLOW_NETWORK`.
